https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4WXYjm74WFI  (Capo 2)

Also presented in G which is easier to fingerpick.

TIP:  To pick out the steel guitar intro notes pick the open 5th string (a), 5th string/2nd fret (b), and 5th string/4th fret (c#).  Then, if you can - the notes come quickly and the move to the first chord is fast -- extend your pinky out to the 5th fret for the first (DaddA).  Otherwise just play (D).  And if transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (DaddA) adding the 5th note as necessary.  Same thing in the two instrumental bridges. 


